TASK
Add a stable move-to-front function for an arbitrary valid sequence index, preserving length and multiset.
Pinned native syntax/toolchain: Dafny 4.4.0+707b18acee078b3aa4d84c0590a980966bf22428; Z3 version 4.12.1 - 64 bit.
The precise fixed source contracts below define correctness. This task adds repodisco-growth/MoveToFront.dfy to the qualified repository.

Return only the replacement body string, not a declaration or an enclosing function/proof block. The host changes only the marked region of MoveToFront. All imports, types, signatures, contracts, specification definitions, termination clauses, other source and build inputs remain fixed.
Body limits: ASCII source; at most 16384 bytes, 4096 lexical tokens and delimiter nesting depth 32. Balanced braces, parentheses and brackets are required. New value locals, expressions, conditionals and assertions are permitted when admitted by the bounded grammar. No source comments, strings/character literals, attributes, new declarations/imports, lambdas/closures, loops, return statements, indirect calls, assumptions, admits, axioms, external/trusted mechanisms, reveal/hide statements, verification options or resource changes. The callable vocabulary is not a required call sequence.
Allowed direct callable names: Model.Swap, MoveToFront, multiset.
Protected inputs: k, xs. Do not assign to or shadow them, or shadow the listed API/type/module/call roots: Model, MoveToFront, Seq, T, bool, int, multiset, nat, u16, u32, u64, u8.
This is a function body and must end with a result expression. Dafny calc blocks are permitted. Use Dafny sequence and multiset syntax; Verus =~= syntax is not allowed. A functional sequence update [index := value] is permitted. Recursive calls are permitted only if listed above and must satisfy the fixed decreases clause.

CURRENT TARGET FILE repodisco-growth/MoveToFront.dfy
```dafny
module RepoDiscoGrowthShift {
  import Model = FisherYates.Model
  export Public provides MoveToFront

  function MoveToFront<T>(xs: seq<T>, k: nat): (ys: seq<T>)
    requires k < |xs|
    ensures ys == [xs[k]] + xs[..k] + xs[k+1..]
    ensures |ys| == |xs|
    ensures multiset(ys) == multiset(xs)
    decreases k
  {
    // BEGIN MODEL BODY
    xs
    // END MODEL BODY
  }
}

```

